The indicator starts **red**, in equilibrium with the normal carbon dioxide level of the air. Add carbon dioxide and it goes **yellow**. Take carbon dioxide away and it goes **purple**. So the colour tells you which process won inside the tube:
**yellow** — respiration only, carbon dioxide added (a leaf in the dark);
**red** — no net change (a leaf at its compensation point, or an empty control tube);
**purple** — photosynthesis faster than respiration, carbon dioxide removed (a leaf in bright light).
